---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Nigel Aukland | Cheese" sideBarActiveItemID="cheese">
  <div class="pb-12 mt-5">
    <div class="text-3xl font-bold">Cheese</div>
    <div class="py-2">
      <p class="mt-3">
        One day I will write about cheese... 🧀 and figure out why this styling has gone awry.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Until then, here is some placeholder copy to better demonstrate layout
        width and spacing across multiple lines of content. From cheddar to
        camembert, the world of cheese is wonderfully diverse and delicious.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Soft-ripened cheeses bloom with character, while hard cheeses deliver a
        concentrated depth of flavor. Washed-rind varieties bring bold aromas,
        and blue cheeses strike a balance between tang and creaminess.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3">
        <li>Cheddar: sharp, crumbly, versatile</li>
        <li>Gouda: nutty, caramel notes, great for melting</li>
        <li>Brie: creamy, buttery, mild rind</li>
        <li>Roquefort: tangy, blue-veined, assertive</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

